{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "grype",
          "version": "0.118.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-19931-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-19931 medium vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in libcurl makes it wrongly reuse an HTTP connection setup for a given\nhostname using Negotiate authentication, when the initial request is done\nusing empty credentials. This can make user B's request get sent over user A's\npreviously authenticated connection."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-19931",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-19931\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-19931](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-19931)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-19931**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | curl  | 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-19931](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-19931)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/curl@8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-19931-libcurl4t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-19931 medium vulnerability for libcurl4t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in libcurl makes it wrongly reuse an HTTP connection setup for a given\nhostname using Negotiate authentication, when the initial request is done\nusing empty credentials. This can make user B's request get sent over user A's\npreviously authenticated connection."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-19931",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-19931\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nVersion: 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-19931](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-19931)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-19931**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libcurl4t64  | 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-19931](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-19931)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libcurl4t64@8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-18924-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-18924 medium vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in libcurl's handling of HTTP/2 Server Push streams, when the parent\nhandle is set to share connections with other handles, can lead to\nuse-after-free in the cleanup process."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-18924",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-18924\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-18924](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-18924)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-18924**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | curl  | 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-18924](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-18924)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/curl@8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-18924-libcurl4t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-18924 medium vulnerability for libcurl4t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in libcurl's handling of HTTP/2 Server Push streams, when the parent\nhandle is set to share connections with other handles, can lead to\nuse-after-free in the cleanup process."
