                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-18924**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libcurl4t64  | 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-18924](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-18924)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libcurl4t64@8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-13608-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-13608 medium vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in the libcurl SASL negotiation for LDAP authentication allows an\nincomplete handshake sequence to be misinterpreted as a successful\ncryptographic verification. An attacker executing a Man-in-the-Middle (MITM)\nattack can inject a premature or shortcut response that bypasses complete peer\nvalidation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-13608",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-13608\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-13608](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-13608)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-13608**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | curl  | 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-13608](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-13608)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/curl@8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.4"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-13608-libcurl4t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-13608 medium vulnerability for libcurl4t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in the libcurl SASL negotiation for LDAP authentication allows an\nincomplete handshake sequence to be misinterpreted as a successful\ncryptographic verification. An attacker executing a Man-in-the-Middle (MITM)\nattack can inject a premature or shortcut response that bypasses complete peer\nvalidation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-13608",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-13608\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nVersion: 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-13608](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-13608)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-13608**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libcurl4t64  | 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-13608](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-13608)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libcurl4t64@8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.4"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80230-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-80230 medium vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When `CURLOPT_PINNEDPUBLICKEY` is configured alongside options that disable\nstandard peer verification (`CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER = 0` and\n`CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYHOST = 0`), libcurl fails to enforce public key pinning on\nconnections established without a presented server certificate. Bypassing the\npinning check under these disabled-verification conditions allows\nunauthenticated connections to succeed when they should be rejected."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-80230",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80230\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-80230](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-80230)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80230**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | curl  | 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-80230](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-80230)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/curl@8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80230-libcurl4t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-80230 medium vulnerability for libcurl4t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When `CURLOPT_PINNEDPUBLICKEY` is configured alongside options that disable\nstandard peer verification (`CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER = 0` and\n`CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYHOST = 0`), libcurl fails to enforce public key pinning on\nconnections established without a presented server certificate. Bypassing the\npinning check under these disabled-verification conditions allows\nunauthenticated connections to succeed when they should be rejected."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-80230",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80230\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nVersion: 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-80230](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-80230)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80230**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libcurl4t64  | 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-80230](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-80230)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libcurl4t64@8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-82209-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-82209 medium vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When libpsl support is enabled, libcurl fails to enforce the Public Suffix\nList boundary check when processing a `Set-Cookie` header where the `Domain`\nattribute explicitly matches an origin host that is itself a public suffix\n(e.g., `Domain=co.uk` set by `co.uk`).\n\nInstead of coercing it into a strict host-only cookie, libcurl saves the\ncookie with wildcard domain scope (`.co.uk`). Consequently, the cookie is\ninappropriately included in subsequent outbound requests or HTTP redirects to\narbitrary sibling subdomains under the same public suffix (e.g.,\n`attacker.co.uk`)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-82209",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-82209\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-82209](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-82209)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-82209**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | curl  | 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-82209](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-82209)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/curl@8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-82209-libcurl4t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-82209 medium vulnerability for libcurl4t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When libpsl support is enabled, libcurl fails to enforce the Public Suffix\nList boundary check when processing a `Set-Cookie` header where the `Domain`\nattribute explicitly matches an origin host that is itself a public suffix\n(e.g., `Domain=co.uk` set by `co.uk`).\n\nInstead of coercing it into a strict host-only cookie, libcurl saves the\ncookie with wildcard domain scope (`.co.uk`). Consequently, the cookie is\ninappropriately included in subsequent outbound requests or HTTP redirects to\narbitrary sibling subdomains under the same public suffix (e.g.,\n`attacker.co.uk`)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-82209",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-82209\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nVersion: 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-82209](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-82209)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-82209**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libcurl4t64  | 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-82209](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-82209)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libcurl4t64@8.5.0-2ubuntu10.13?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-85091-zlib1g",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-85091 medium vulnerability for zlib1g package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "zlib versions 1.3.1.2 through 1.3.2 contain a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the gz_vacate() function when processing non-blocking gzwrite() operations with stale external buffer pointers. Attackers can trigger the overflow by calling gzprintf() or gzvprintf() after a write stall, causing an unchecked memmove() to write beyond the internal input buffer boundary."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-85091",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-85091\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: zlib1g\nVersion: 1:1.3.dfsg-3.1ubuntu2.2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-85091](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-85091)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-85091**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | zlib1g  | 1:1.3.dfsg-3.1ubuntu2.2  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-85091](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-85091)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/zlib1g@1%3A1.3.dfsg-3.1ubuntu2.2?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=zlib"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-19487-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-19487 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Perl versions from 5.9.4 before 5.41.9 produce incorrect regular expression match results when a stale failure flag ends the Aho-Corasick prescan early in S_find_byclass.\n\nThe prescan walks the subject for positions where the full pattern could match, and the engine tries it from the leftmost one recorded. A failing transition sets the failed flag, and a later successful transition does not clear it, so the prescan reads the stale flag as a failure and stops before it can record a candidate that starts earlier. It takes a subject where one candidate is recorded and a later character then forces a fallback through a fail link that succeeds.\n\nExample:\n\n  \"ABCDE\" =~ m/ABCF|BCDE|C/;    # matches C at offset 2, not BCDE\n  \"ABCDE\" =~ m/ABCF|BCDE|C(G)/; # no match, BCDE missed\n\nAn alternation like this can miss input it should match, or match it on the wrong branch, so an access or filtering decision made from the result can be wrong."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-19487",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-19487\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.4\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-19487](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-19487)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-19487**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.4  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-19487](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-19487)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/perl-base@5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.4?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-86145-libpcre2-8-0",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-86145 medium vulnerability for libpcre2-8-0 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "PCRE2 before 10.48 allows a pcre2_dfa_match out-of-bounds write because reuse of a cached workspace block, in a recursive DFA matching workspace, lacks a size check (even though a newly allocated block, for the same purpose, does have a size check). This outcome requires an attacker-controlled regular expression, or a recursive pattern in conjunction with a small heap limit (this can be set through the API)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-86145",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-86145\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libpcre2-8-0\nVersion: 10.42-4ubuntu2.1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-86145](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-86145)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-86145**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libpcre2-8-0  | 10.42-4ubuntu2.1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-86145](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-86145)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libpcre2-8-0@10.42-4ubuntu2.1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=pcre2"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-10041-libpam-modules",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-10041 medium vulnerability for libpam-modules package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A vulnerability was found in PAM. The secret information is stored in memory, where the attacker can trigger the victim program to execute by sending characters to its standard input (stdin). As this occurs, the attacker can train the branch predictor to execute an ROP chain speculatively. This flaw could result in leaked passwords, such as those found in /etc/shadow while performing authentications."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2024-10041",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-10041\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libpam-modules\nVersion: 1.5.3-5ubuntu5.7\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2024-10041](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2024-10041)",
